    "translation.ai.settings.feature.cross-rule-conflict-detection.description": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "ar": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needs_review",
            "value": "Opt-in LLM that reads the typed AlertRule definitions in the current scope (optionally narrowed by vehicle, signal name, enabled-only, or an explicit rule-id list) and surfaces structural conflicts within a closed taxonomy of two kinds: redundant_duplicate (byte-identical predicate plus overlapping vehicle scope, both enabled) and overlapping_threshold (same signal_name, overlapping vehicle scope, predicate intervals overlap on numeric ops). Each surfaced conflict carries metadata flags for severity_mismatch, cooldown_mismatch, trigger_mode_mismatch, and subsumes — informational only, never a new conflict kind. Descriptive structural overlap analysis only — explicitly NOT a prediction — and never edits, merges, or deletes rules; the user clicks Review rule {id} to navigate the AlertStudio editor and applies any change manually. The deterministic AlertStudio rule list and per-rule validation remain the canonical baseline when Helix is off."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Opt-in LLM that reads the typed AlertRule definitions in the current scope (optionally narrowed by vehicle, signal name, enabled-only, or an explicit rule-id list) and surfaces structural conflicts within a closed taxonomy of two kinds: redundant_duplicate (byte-identical predicate plus overlapping vehicle scope, both enabled) and overlapping_threshold (same signal_name, overlapping vehicle scope, predicate intervals overlap on numeric ops). Each surfaced conflict carries metadata flags for severity_mismatch, cooldown_mismatch, trigger_mode_mismatch, and subsumes — informational only, never a new conflict kind. Descriptive structural overlap analysis only — explicitly NOT a prediction — and never edits, merges, or deletes rules; the user clicks Review rule {id} to navigate the AlertStudio editor and applies any change manually. The deterministic AlertStudio rule list and per-rule validation remain the canonical baseline when Helix is off."
          }
        },
        "he": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needs_review",
            "value": "Opt-in LLM that reads the typed AlertRule definitions in the current scope (optionally narrowed by vehicle, signal name, enabled-only, or an explicit rule-id list) and surfaces structural conflicts within a closed taxonomy of two kinds: redundant_duplicate (byte-identical predicate plus overlapping vehicle scope, both enabled) and overlapping_threshold (same signal_name, overlapping vehicle scope, predicate intervals overlap on numeric ops). Each surfaced conflict carries metadata flags for severity_mismatch, cooldown_mismatch, trigger_mode_mismatch, and subsumes — informational only, never a new conflict kind. Descriptive structural overlap analysis only — explicitly NOT a prediction — and never edits, merges, or deletes rules; the user clicks Review rule {id} to navigate the AlertStudio editor and applies any change manually. The deterministic AlertStudio rule list and per-rule validation remain the canonical baseline when Helix is off."
